<html>
  <head>
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=Cp1252">
    <meta name="generator" content="Helen">
    <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="../../../../javahelp.css">
    <title>Modifying network properties</title>
  </head>
  <body bgcolor="#ffffff">
    <h1>
       <img border="0" hspace="0" s7starttagpos="284" height="32" width="32" src=
      "../../../../images/carmenHelpIcons/c3_32.gif">&nbsp;&nbsp; Modifying network properties
    </h1>
    <table border="1" cellpadding="4" cellspacing="0" bordercolor="#000000" width="490">
      <col width="235">
      <col width="237">
      <tr>
        <td colspan="2" valign="top" width="480">
          <p>
             <b><font size="3">Use case: Modifying network properties</font></b>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td colspan="2" valign="top" width="480">
          <p>
             <b><font size="3">Comment:</font></b> <font size="3">The properties of a network can
            be changed in any moment of execution, using the following steps.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td colspan="2" valign="top" width="480">
          <p>
             <b><font size="3">Actor: User</font></b>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="235">
          <p>
             <b><font size="3">Normal course</font></b>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p>
             <b><font size="3">Alternative courses</font></b>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="235">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">1.When the type of editing is the selection of objects, the user double
            presses on the empty background of the network panel which is in the main menu or in
            the pop-up menu.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="235">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">2.A dialog box appears where the properties of the network can be
            modified excepting its type and type of variables of the nodes.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="235">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">3.The user changes the properties by writing or selecting new
            values.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">3.1.The user can cancel the operation so the use case will end.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="235">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">4.The user accepts the properties changes.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">4.1.The user can cancel the operation so the use case will end.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="235">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">5.The program checks if the data given by the user are correct.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">5.1.If a data is not correct, the program informs the user and goes to
            point 3.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="235">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">6.If the name of the network has been changed, the window title will be
            showed where the user is editing and in the window list of the multi-document
            environment dependant menu in the main menu.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="235">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">7.A new point to undo and redo the modification of the network
            properties is created.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="235">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">8.The use case <i>Updating menus when modifying a network</i> is
            executed.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" align=
          "left">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="235">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">9.The network is marked as modified (if it was not already), placing an
            asterisk at the title of the window in which is being editing.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="237">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" align=
          "left">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
    <p>
       &nbsp;
    </p>
  </body>
</html>
